    title: 'Riverside Fitness & Aquatic Centre: Member Handbook',
    sectionNumber: 1,
    wordCount: 420,
    body: `Welcome to Riverside Fitness & Aquatic Centre, the newest leisure facility in Overton Borough. This handbook explains our membership options, opening hours, and the rules that apply to all members and their guests. Please keep a copy for reference, as it forms part of your membership agreement.

Opening Hours
The centre is open from 6:00 a.m. to 10:00 p.m. Monday to Friday, and from 7:00 a.m. to 8:00 p.m. on Saturdays and Sundays. The swimming pool closes thirty minutes before the rest of the centre to allow time for cleaning. On public holidays the centre operates reduced hours, from 9:00 a.m. to 4:00 p.m., and this schedule is posted at reception two weeks in advance.

Membership Types
We offer three membership categories. The Bronze membership, priced at £28 per month, grants access to the gymnasium and the group exercise studio only. The Silver membership, at £42 per month, includes everything in Bronze plus unlimited use of the swimming pool and sauna. The Gold membership, at £59 per month, includes everything in Silver plus two free personal training sessions each month and priority booking for the group exercise studio, which can otherwise fill up quickly during peak evening hours. All memberships require a minimum commitment of one month, and new members must complete a short induction session with a member of staff before using the gymnasium equipment for the first time.

Guest Policy
Members may bring up to two guests per visit, provided the guest is signed in at reception and accompanied at all times. Guests are charged a flat fee of £8 per visit, payable at reception, and may not bring guests of their own. Children under fourteen are not permitted in the gymnasium at any time, though those aged eight and above may use the swimming pool if accompanied by a paying adult member.

Cancellations and Refunds
Membership may be cancelled at any time after the first month by giving thirty days written notice to reception or by email to the membership office. Refunds are not offered for partial months. Members who cancel and later wish to rejoin within six months will be charged the standard £15 joining fee again, whereas members who rejoin after more than six months are exempt from this fee as a welcome-back incentive.

Locker Rooms and Lost Property
Lockers are available on a daily-use basis only; members should bring their own padlock, as any lock left overnight without prior arrangement will be cut off and its contents moved to lost property. Lost property is held for twenty-eight days before being donated to a local charity.`,
