    id: '22000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000004',
    ieltsType: 'general',
    title: 'Willowbrook Holiday Park: Guest Information and House Rules',
    sectionNumber: 1,
    wordCount: 430,
    body: `Welcome to Willowbrook Holiday Park. We hope you enjoy your stay in one of our forty-two self-catering lodges, set within twelve acres of woodland beside the River Calder. Please read the following information carefully, as it forms part of the booking conditions you agreed to when reserving your lodge.

Check-in and Check-out
Check-in is from 3:00 p.m. on the day of arrival; lodges cannot be accessed before this time under any circumstances, as our housekeeping team requires the full day to prepare each lodge between guests. Check-out is by 10:00 a.m. on the day of departure. Guests requiring a later check-out should ask at reception at least twenty-four hours in advance; a late check-out until 12 noon can be arranged for a fee of £15, subject to availability.

Parking and Vehicles
Each lodge is allocated one parking space directly outside the property. Guests bringing a second vehicle must park in the overflow car park near the entrance and should register the vehicle's registration number at reception on arrival. The speed limit throughout the park is 10 miles per hour at all times, strictly enforced to protect the many families with young children who walk freely around the site.

Pets
Well-behaved dogs are welcome in designated pet-friendly lodges only, of which there are eighteen across the park; a supplement of £25 per stay applies per dog, with a maximum of two dogs per lodge. Dogs must be kept on a lead at all times outside the lodge and are not permitted inside the swimming pool building, the restaurant, or the children's play barn. Owners must clean up after their pets immediately; failure to do so may result in the loss of the deposit.

Fires and Barbecues
Open fires are not permitted anywhere on the park. Barbecues may be used only on the paved area immediately outside each lodge, using the barbecue provided, and must never be left unattended while lit. During periods of high fire risk, which are announced on the park noticeboard and website, barbecue use may be temporarily suspended for all guests.

Noise and Quiet Hours
To ensure all guests enjoy a peaceful stay, quiet hours apply between 11:00 p.m. and 8:00 a.m., during which amplified music and loud outdoor activity are not permitted. Guests who repeatedly breach quiet hours may be asked to leave without a refund.

Damage and Deposits
A refundable security deposit of £100 is taken at booking and returned within seven working days of departure, provided no damage or excessive cleaning is required.`,
